{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two","id":981889,"title":"Gecko's Awakening Hack, Take Two","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-04T18:42:37-07:00","id":981889,"title":"Gecko's Awakening Hack, Take Two","content":"Making a new thread, as was suggested: <br /> <br /> I've been wondering if there was a way to accomplish my goals for Mage: The Transgression on a smaller scale, by slightly hacking and nudging Awakening. The primary goal isn't just to make it more fun or flavorful or mad science-y, but to emphasize the personal horror elements as much as possible. The most important thing is, what would be the best way to run or hack Mage in order to emphasize the ambiguity and horror of the setting? To really make the players question everything, and to create the genuine possibility that a lot of the principles of the setting are either false or much more complicated. The books raise this, but what would it take to make it a central feature of the setting?<br /> <br /> Here are my goals/ideas so far: <br /> <br /> \u2022 The main thing I want to do is present being Awakening as a cursed, monstrous condition rather than a blessing, and make it plausible that close to or more than half of Mages wish secretly or openly that they were normal humans again. <br /> \u2022 Paradox and Obsessions both being much more dangerous and punishing would help. <br /> \u2022 Archmastery is equivalent to becoming a True Fae- the Mage becomes an utterly inhuman entity. <br /> \u2022 There's a lot of Genius influence. The Pentacle, for example, gets a LOT of influence from the Lemurians. <br /> \u2022 As Mages gain power and lose Wisdom, they might take Bans and Banes related to how they can perform magic, like other supernatural creatures. <br /> \u2022 The subjective nature of the Supernal is emphasized, as well as the possibility that it's essentially a shared delusion that Mages can force into reality. Players only have to pick one of their Path's Arcana, and choose any other as their second ruling Arcana. Experiences of the Supernal realms are vastly different and subjective. <br /> \u2022 Some Mages have no Path. They are stereotyped as being more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but the truth of this assumption is questionable. <br /> \u2022 A significant and ever-increasing number of Mages Awaken as Gifted Scientists from the Mage Chronicler's Guide, because I really really want to emphasize mad scientists as much as possible, since they're pretty much the modern version of the &quot;sorcerer as monster&quot; archetype. <br /> <br /> Feedback and suggestions are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:44:20-07:00","id":981891,"title":"","content":"\u2022 Many Mages deliberately try to avoid gaining power, because gaining power inevitably removes the Mage more and more from humanity. Obsessions get stronger, Bans and Banes develop, and ultimately the Mage risks becoming an utterly inhuman Archmaster. <br /> \u2022 Mages are stuck between the risk of higher power and the painful compulsion to seek it- their Obsessions constantly force them to delve into paranormal phenomena and seek knowledge, no matter how much they try to resist. <br /> \u2022 The Nimbus grows more powerful as a Mage gains in power as a representation of their growing distance from humanity, acting similarly to the Wake from Leviathan. <br /> \u2022 It's quite hard to effect powerful supernatural creatures, and some are immune to direct uses of magic entirely. Creativity and problem-solving are key. <br /> \u2022 More pessimistic Mages prefer the terms &quot;Hollow&quot; or &quot;Open&quot; to &quot;Awakened&quot;, because they more accurately describe what happens. A Mage blows a hole in his soul and desperately fills it with chunks of occult symbols, grabbing onto a watchtower to survive having their mind cast into primordial chaos. The &quot;hollow&quot; nature of Mages is why they're so sensitive to the occult and potent with it: they have &quot;open space&quot; with which to connect directly with the supernatural. Obsessions play into this, too: every Mage feels a deep and aching pain, as if they are missing something precious, and Obsessions are an attempt to fill that hole. <br /> \u2022 The factions now have more of a resemblance to the Covenants in Vampire- they primarily exist to help Mages justify and survive their cursed state. <br /> \u2022 The Silver Ladder is sort of equivalent to the Invictus, using elaborate hierarchies and rituals to manage their condition. They try to frame the Awakened state as a honorable burden, something given only to the worthy. Members of this group are most likely to be Lemurians- those who are trying to bring back a lost magical golden age. <br /> \u2022 The Mysterium seek knowledge with a fervor that surpasses that of other Mages. Some seek it for its own sake, while others look for the secrets of the world in the hope of regulating or removing their condition. They study the past to learn from it. Most historically significant Mages, after all, are primarily famous as cautionary tales. <br /> \u2022 The Guardians of the Veil know just how dangerous the supernatural is, especially the volatile powers of their own kind. They dedicate themselves completely to protecting the Whole not just from direct menaces but from knowledge that might lead them down the same self-destructive path the Hollow tread. <br /> \u2022 The Adamantine Arrow are not simply about warfare or strength. They focus on control and refinement as a means of honing mind and body to withstand the ravages of the Awakened condition. Many are in some way ascetic, seeking enough control to keep the fires raging inside them under control. <br /> \u2022 The Free Council are no longer the primary technomages at all. Every order has a fair proportion of scientifically-focused mages and Gifted Scientists. The Council's connection to mortal occult traditions is much more important to them, because their focus is connection: remaining in contact with the mortal world and humanity so as to avoid drifting away from it. <br /> \u2022 I've always disliked how the most human splat was the most powerful one, so having to choose between being human or being powerful is a major theme. <br /> \u2022 Hm, maybe The Hollow Chronicle is a good name for it. <br /> \u2022 No player is allowed to make a character inspired by Dr. Who or Benedict Cumberbatch's Sherlock. Any character who qualifies as a sarcastic british man is to be subject to close ST scrutiny, and is only allowed a maximum of three quips per game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:52:31-07:00","id":981895,"title":"","content":"*sigh*<br /> <br /> You might want to review those two posts for anything that might come across as pre-emptively defensive, or attacking styles of play or preferences that disagree with your own. If you can't see the problematic parts of these two posts without being told what they are, I don't have high hopes for this thread going any better than the last one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:08:00-07:00","id":981904,"title":"","content":"Like I was saying at the end of the previous thread, if magic is cursed and something Mages deliberately want to avoid then why do they even cast spells? What stops them from just not doing magic? The changes you seek to make need to be gameable, and this question and its answer is the foundation to everything else you should be editing. It's summed up in this point you post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=981891#post981891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Mages are stuck between the risk of higher power and the painful compulsion to seek it- their Obsessions constantly force them to delve into paranormal phenomena and seek knowledge, no matter how much they try to resist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked why do Mages even cast spells and your answer, seemingly, is that Obsessions push them to do it. Fine; someone did suggest using Obsessions as a 'stick' rather than the 'carrot' they're currently written as. There's nothing inherently wrong with this.<br /> <br /> The important point to realize here is that it needs to be gameable. Will your <i>players </i>want to <i>play</i> someone who is <i>forced</i> to use magic that is <i>cursed</i> and that they would ideally seek to <i>avoid</i>? Will Obsessions as a stick be <i>fun</i> for your players (or other potential audiences)?<br /> <br /> Vampires, werewolves, and other monsters who have inhuman compulsions are fun for players because, long story short, XP incentives (narrative incentive exists but is rewarded in <b>CofD</b> by beats). Is it <i>fun</i> for players to be near-forced to have to use their magic? Can they choose <i>not </i>to use their magic despite the stick of Obsession?<br /> <br /> If <i>that's</i> the case then it's a game of choice and what your players' Mages choose to do with their magic, making the best of it. Isn't that just what <b>Mage the Awakening</b> is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:11:59-07:00","id":981922,"title":"","content":"The first Mage book I worked on back in 1st Ed. was Night Horrors: The Unbidden. It was mostly a monsters book, but sort of the central inspiration was that magic wasn't something mages had all figured out. Sometimes it came unbidden into the world, and mages had to sort it out. It sounds like your notion of mages as cursed even more than they are blessed follows that particular train of thought (albeit not one I've seen a whole lot of in the past or present line). Reseru is correct to point out that the trick is finding a group that will find that kind of spin evocative and fun and not needlessly punitive or adversarial. Assuming they're on board, here's one I'd consider low-hanging fruit:<br /> <br /> Take a page out of Beast's Satiety system. When Wisdom gets low because the mage is flinging around sorcery in ways that endanger everyone around him, that's its own kind of problem (amply covered in the current mechanics, really). However, make it so that if a mage goes without using magic (and without Reaching regularly) her Wisdom keeps climbing. That's good, right? No. That's bad, too. A mage is a pore between the Fallen World and the Supernal World, and if that pore gets clogged by a wizard who refuses to function properly (using magic), it becomes infected and pressurized until, eventually, it explodes in an unsightly and painful flow of puss and blood.<br /> <br /> This is the point at which it resembles Beast. A high-Wisdom mage's unused magic eventually leaks into the world, causing trouble in the mage's vicinity that reflects her Long-Term Nimbus as it tear tiny holes in reality through which unguided Supernal power and the poisons of the Abyss leak into the world. Mechanically, Anomalies start showing up the region where the high-Wisdom mage lives. The higher her Gnosis, the wider the range of those Anomalies. The higher her Wisdom, the worse those Anomalies (gradually worsening into Manifestations) become.<br /> <br /> This one would be comparatively easy to implement without a ton of mechanical changes. It doesn't require you to create Bans/Banes or rewrite the magic system. That said, you can certainly hammer out some mechanical reflection of the Supernal &quot;pressure&quot; building up in a mage.<br /> <br /> You can head off the &quot;obvious&quot; solution by saying that whenever one mage dies, another Awakens. Yeah, it still behooves you to off particularly bad mages, but when facing sliiiighly awful ones you're taking the risk that the ones who replace them will be <i>worse</i>.<br /> <br /> Okay, here's one more random one - not as thought-out, however: Maybe just using magic alone isn't enough to keep Wisdom under control. Perhaps Obsessions function a little bit like Shadow Names - but instead of keeping Nimbus from leaking out into the mage's mundane life they give her an excuse to use lots of magic to accomplish some moderately Quixotic goal. Maybe just throwing down and winning the lottery isn't enough of an act of hubris to keep the monsters from crawling out of the walls, but using magic to manage the lives of a family of Sleepers so that little baby Kate grows up to marry a Charlie (your obsession doesn't care which Charlie she marries - only that his name is Charlie) - or something equally arcane - helps reduce the magical pressure. Is it better to brainwash dozens of innocent people to prevent an Abyssal pandemic from sweeping across the country, or do you feel better about yourself if you're just manipulating one specific person or family in a really up-close, personal, and in-no-way-accidental way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:33:34-07:00","id":981931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=981922#post981922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, make it so that if a mage goes without using magic (and without Reaching regularly) her Wisdom keeps climbing. That's good, right? No. That's bad, too. A mage is a pore between the Fallen World and the Supernal World, and if that pore gets clogged by a wizard who refuses to function properly (using magic), it becomes infected and pressurized until, eventually, it explodes in an unsightly and painful flow of puss and blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this could be more tidily managed by just hacking the mechanics for the Mad to apply to a wider subset of mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:43:42-07:00","id":981935,"title":"","content":"#NimbusCanAlwaysBeABiggerShitstorm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:58:17-07:00","id":981939,"title":"","content":"This is a &quot;setting&quot;/storyteller suggestion, but amp up the Long-Term Nimbus so that it starts doing stuff at lower levels of Gnosis (start it at 3 or something maybe rather than 6?). Write up a list of examples for yourself as a push-off point for every &quot;Path&quot; (Primary from a Path + that one that people can pick for themselves) increasing in severity in accordance to gnosis, as this is the mechanism by which you're suppose to have mages unconsciously warp reality around them into doom. Based on how wisdom works with nimbus, starting-level mages have it taint and curse their siblings and friends and objects they have emotional connection with already. An acanthus's baby sister seems to not get any older than 3, and his dead father's watch seems to keep stopping on the exact second you first found out about his demise. A magistos finds her girlfriend suddenly unable to feel an emotion like fear, because the mage kept thinking &quot;I wish she could stand up to her jerk of a boss&quot; until their nimbus slowly started to chain up the girlfriends fear-goetia. A moros starts to become depressed and broken as all the mementos and photos of his lost family members start decaying, rusting, and fading. Obrimos accidentally gives her husband heart problems as his nervous system keeps having minor surges of electricity out of nowhere. Thyrsus's life energy slowly draws in insects until every inch of their family home's walls hides some form of creepy crawly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-05-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:18:39-07:00","id":981948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=981931#post981931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this could be more tidily managed by just hacking the mechanics for the Mad to apply to a wider subset of mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. Making Obsessions into Faults and using Occultation and Tulpas to force pursuit of those Obsessions is an even simpler solution. I guess I was trying to incorporate Wisdom and hubris into it somehow and was coming up a bit short. Also, I'll admit I've become a bit enamored with the idea of Anomalies that hurt innocent people rather than inconveniencing the mage herself. It seems a bit more horrifying to me than some of the more standard options. Granted, it wouldn't be too hard for a ST to orchestrate ways in which a trail of innocent victims of a mage's out-of-control magic serves as a trail of breadcrumbs leading him back to his neglected fascination with transforming animals into sapient beings (or whatever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:08:09-07:00","id":982007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=981935#post981935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#NimbusCanAlwaysBeABiggerShitstorm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't read the other thread; did anyone suggest hacking Nimbus to use Wasteland mechanics yet? I'm too lazy to actually build that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T06:16:23-07:00","id":982088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two#post981889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The main thing I want to do is present being Awakening as a cursed, monstrous condition rather than a blessing, and make it plausible that close to or more than half of Mages wish secretly or openly that they were normal humans again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can emphasize with this desire, I'd recommend you to read Banishers, Intruders and Left-Hand Path. If you haven't read them already or you don't have them, I'd gladly spend my money on them for you, because I admit, your many threads about this topic has made me really impressed with your dedication to this project, so I'll help you where I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two#post981889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Paradox and Obsessions both being much more dangerous and punishing would help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsessions can be made more dangerous if you emphasize that they should put someone at risk, Paradox might be reworked to be something like an unholy combination of Wasteland and Ascension's Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two#post981889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Archmastery is equivalent to becoming a True Fae- the Mage becomes an utterly inhuman entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Dance Macabre, there is an alternative system called Inhumanity that allows you to modify your Humanity sins every time you encounter one, so you'll end up as something completely inhuman and possibly horrible. I also know you like transhuman themes, so you might make the journey to Archmastery about becoming something that is ultimately <i>posthuman</i>, because you should totally still be allowed to play an Archmaster, you should just be incentivized to act inhuman and weird.<br /> <br /> Perhaps one cannot become an Archmaster before having switched to Inhumanity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two#post981889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 There's a lot of Genius influence. The Pentacle, for example, gets a LOT of influence from the Lemurians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like Genius, but it's your game so go for it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two#post981889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 As Mages gain power and lose Wisdom, they might take Bans and Banes related to how they can perform magic, like other supernatural creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two#post981889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The subjective nature of the Supernal is emphasized, as well as the possibility that it's essentially a shared delusion that Mages can force into reality. Players only have to pick one of their Path's Arcana, and choose any other as their second ruling Arcana. Experiences of the Supernal realms are vastly different and subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I kind of do this myself so go for it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd take a look at <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a>'s Mage homebrew. It's really good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two#post981889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Some Mages have no Path. They are stereotyped as being more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but the truth of this assumption is questionable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, this one seems reasonable.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two#post981889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 A significant and ever-increasing number of Mages Awaken as Gifted Scientists from the Mage Chronicler's Guide, because I really really want to emphasize mad scientists as much as possible, since they're pretty much the modern version of the &quot;sorcerer as monster&quot; archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would recommend you to instead say that the symbolism a mage encounters during her Awakening is extremely variable so that people who like having Mad Scientists can have their kick from that, and people (like me) who want to be psychics that transcend mortal limitations with the untapped potential of the human mind can become that.<br /> <br /> Not full-on Paradigm, but kind of close. Again, take a look at PenDragon's homebrew hub.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:44:59-07:00","id":982239,"title":"","content":"The mages you want seem like a mix of the Mad and banishers. You could see left handed path and banishers for ideas.<br /> For power brings insanity, you could make that 10 - gnosis = max wisdom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:43:25-07:00","id":982272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=982239#post982239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mages you want seem like a mix of the Mad and banishers. You could see left handed path and banishers for ideas.<br /> For power brings insanity, you could make that 10 - gnosis = max wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is extremely elegant but I'd go with 10-(RndDown(gnosis/2)), so your max Wisdom is<br /> <br /> 10<br /> 9<br /> 9<br /> 8<br /> 8<br /> 7<br /> 7<br /> 6<br /> 6<br /> 5<br /> <br /> Otherwise it's just weird since no one can have wisdom 10 and a Gnosis 10 Mage is automatically Mad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:06:03-07:00","id":982288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=982272#post982272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise it's just weird since no one can have wisdom 10 and a Gnosis 10 Mage is automatically Mad</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would suit gecko preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:52:21-07:00","id":982369,"title":"","content":"If you want to make mage more personal horror you could get rid of the orders, if there are no spanning organisations to give answers, explanations and theory every local group and mage need yo figure everything out by themselves.<br /> <br /> What if every spell comes with a price? I mean some sort of paradox. You could take some inspiration from dresden files, the player choses a cursed theme for their character, in Harrys case it is magic screws thecnology.<br /> Ehen harry cast his first spell for the day he can't use technology. After the second spell the person closest to him is also afflicted and it escalates from there.<br /> For a mage with another tecnology hhem: after the firdt dpell the characters tecnology starts fokng things on its own. Another mage could be marked as a witch in more and more obvius ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:49:53-07:00","id":982486,"title":"","content":"I also wonder why OP wants to use <b>Mage the Awakening</b> even as the template for the hack. A lot of its mechanics rely heavily on the nature of the setting and it's almost like so much would have to be different you're better off using a different game.<br /> <br /> There's so many other games out there about sorcerers, it's not as if there's zero room for a game that covers <b>Awakening</b>'s themes, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:41:47-07:00","id":982515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=982486#post982486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wonder why OP wants to use <b>Mage the Awakening</b> even as the template for the hack. A lot of its mechanics rely heavily on the nature of the setting and it's almost like so much would have to be different you're better off using a different game.<br /> <br /> There's so many other games out there about sorcerers, it's not as if there's zero room for a game that covers <b>Awakening</b>'s themes, too</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of feel her pain. The magic system in Awakening remains my gold standard. I've never seen anything quite get the mix of creative thaumaturgy and hundreds of example spells exactly right, and every time I try to conjure one from scratch I can't escape its influence. I've been tinkering with game systems for decades, and no game seems quite so perfect for hacking, modifying, and repurposing to meet my current gaming goals. It's just so...comprehensive.<br /> <br /> I had fun toying with Buffy and Ascension, BESM and FATE look pretty good on paper, and I'll always have a bit of a nostalgia for D&amp;D (2nd Ed and earlier), but I keep finding myself returning to Awakening's combination of endless variation and (mostly) clear guidelines for building new spells. I'd rather take that engine and build a completely new car around it than shop around for a dream setting only to find that their mechanics either actively discourage creativity or abandon me in a sea of GM fiat with nary a hand wave.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the system is pretty intimately tied to the setting, and if you want to make major changes the latter, you're going to have make some changes to the former. And you might come up with some clever and cool mechanical solutions to the problems your setting changes create, but some of those problems aren't easy to solve, and not every mechanical patch actually works the way you intended. It can indeed feel a bit like how an Obsession must feel to a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:50:10-07:00","id":982518,"title":"","content":"I have often wondered if Mage were real if the game system that modeled it would be my Obsession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T04:06:01-07:00","id":982635,"title":"","content":"In order to ignore an Obsession, the Mage needs to succeed on a Wisdom roll first. If it fails, he can only pull away after committing an Act of Hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:28:02-07:00","id":990253,"title":"","content":"Sorry it took me so long to get back! All of those are good ideas. <br /> <br /> As another bit of setting philosophy and to put things in Genius terms, the Diamond should be sort of like Lemuria and the Free Council should be sort of like the Peerage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:58:17-07:00","id":990308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=981895#post981895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*sigh*<br /> <br /> You might want to review those two posts for anything that might come across as pre-emptively defensive, or attacking styles of play or preferences that disagree with your own. If you can't see the problematic parts of these two posts without being told what they are, I don't have high hopes for this thread going any better than the last one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. One of the most glaring changes in tone between the the oWod Mage first edition and revised was the way they tried to make it about 'street level games' by making the horizon realms far less playable. The person who introduced me to Mage said that it ruined revised for her and she stuck with 1st edition. Learn to embody a 'yes, and' mentality, and if you want to run a game a certain way get agreements from the players on how the game will run rather than force it mechanically. For example if you don't want to run a 'Pink Mohawk' Shadowrun game, spell that out before hand rather than saying &quot;Lone Star will come down on violent criminals with excessive force.&quot; That way all the players and the GM will be on the same page as each other, that way if one player has different desires or expectations you can work with them and try and come up with a way to satisfy all parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10831-bauran","name":"Bauran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10831_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T00:10:40-07:00","id":990313,"title":"","content":"O...kay...we kinda worked that out a while ago, and I even edited the post because of it. Do you have any suggestions for the project?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T04:55:45-07:00","id":990371,"title":"","content":"Play Banishers. Have regular mages be the bad guys, and the reason that your characters use their magic at all. It's the only tool they have to defeat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:09:16-07:00","id":990414,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not going to be doing that. I'd rather just change a few things and make the regular setup of Pentacle vs the Seers closer to my own preferences. We've gotten quite a bit done already, how does it look to you so far?<br /> <br /> I certainly want to raise the possibility that the Banishers are right, or more right than wrong, in the way that Leviathan permits that Ahabs and Marduk might very well be right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:21:44-07:00","id":991681,"title":"","content":"So, I'm thinking of including some new legacies as part of the text of the hack. The two I have so far are a Silver Ladder legacy of deist clockwork-obsessed utopia seekers, an open Legacy of wannabe supervillains, and their rivals/predecessors, an Acanthus legacy known as the Foils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T21:35:28-07:00","id":991706,"title":"","content":"Another major consideration: what makes mages &quot;lesser&quot; than baseline humans? Why would someone not want to become a mage? Why would a minor template sorcerer not want to become a mage? Why would a mage want to become human again?<br /> <br /> I really want to push the &quot;living hole in reality&quot; thing as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:20:26-07:00","id":991718,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be neat if Legacies had weaknesses, like Bloodlines. The one I like the most is that when a Mage joins a legacy it's much harder to perform magic without using their Paradigm or practice. <br /> <br /> For example, the clockworkers can only use clockwork machinery to focus their magic, and supervillains have to choose a &quot;theme&quot; and stick with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:05:36-07:00","id":991741,"title":"","content":"Hi Geckopirateship! I think your project to rework Promethean and Mage is pretty interesting, so I'd love to see how it turns out. I guess for your legacies I'm a mixed bag. I think silver ladder utopians who use matter is pretty decent. Maybe the thing to emphasize is their belief that just creating a perfect system of material devices and conveniences will lead to enlightenment running up against human weaknesses and divisions? I actually had been mulling over the idea of a Foil-like Acanthus legacy before reading your material, so I definitely like the idea. It seems like they'd make great fits for the Adamantine Arrow.<br /> <br /> The thing i can't really see is the supervillain legacy group. It just seems like there a lot of problems with having an entire set of legacies for different paths all of which are committed to a single character archetype. How broad are we talking for &quot;supervillain&quot;? Is this only 4-color villains like The Lizard and Doctor Doom? James Bond style millionaire sadists? Herbert Wests? Sure, there are several concepts here, but having them be THE major successor to a legacy of generalist foils and rivals feels limiting to me. &quot;Modern villains&quot; even of the mostly human group includes Magneto sure, but also Michael Myers, Sith Lords, and the Cobra Kai from Karate Kid. Plus given how obvious I imagine their acts can be, you'd have to address how they keep up their numbers in the face of mages and supernatural creatures they'd piss off<br /> <br /> its possible I'm getting the legacy wrong, of course. I'm going by what I remember from another forum thread discussing legacies in more detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:20:58-07:00","id":991748,"title":"","content":"Well, generally they cover any concept you could imagine seeing as a comic book villain. Have you ever seen The Venture Brothers? They're basically the Guild of Calamitous Intent. I kind of feel like if it made it any broader, it wouldn't really have any thematic coherence.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m.reddit.com/r/AskScienceFiction/comments/3m4tdu/venture_bros_so_whats_the_purpose_of_the_guild_of/\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.reddit.com/r/AskScienceFic..._the_guild_of/</a> Here's an explanation of what purpose the Guild serves, which explains why the Pentacle would put up with it. The Seers don't like them, however, because the Seers like things stable and hopeless, and superheroes and villains squaring off is something of an obstacle to that. <br /> <br /> Same reason they wouldn't like the Foils. The Seers don't like thinking in terms of good guys and bad guys, and they don't like the general population thinking that way. They'd prefer that the dominant paradigm was &quot;incomprehensibly powerful and faceless dominion and average joes who know to shut the fuck up and not make trouble&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-23-2016, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:33:38-07:00","id":991753,"title":"","content":"Point taken, legacies do need a clear theme and &quot;all villains&quot; is too broad. Never seen Venture Bros., so I'd need to think more about how such a group would appeal to and attract new members.<br /> <br /> Actually, that brings up another point - if you want to emphasize that Awakening is curse and many mages want to be cured, where does that leave legacies? Even the ones that aren't explicitly transhumanist are basically all about becoming a more inherently magical being, so by the hacked metaphysics shouldn't lots of mages see that as a drawback? Perhaps legacy soul-shaping is believed to repair the damage done by awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:38:13-07:00","id":991755,"title":"","content":"That could work. And I mean, &quot;this is a curse&quot; isn't a universal drawback, and plenty of mages still try to make the most of it. One of the themes I'm working with is voids and hollowness- mages hollow out their souls to turn them into Supernal conduits, and embracing legacies and personas and so on makes up for that. And then there's the fact that mages genuinely have a hard time avoiding pursuing magical knowledge, due to Obsessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:06:41-07:00","id":992041,"title":"","content":"Some more thoughts:<br /> <br /> My personal canon is that all formerly human supernatural beings could technically be considered Deviants, and Deviant deals with the incidences of deviance that aren't structured or numerous enough to be part of an existing category. <br /> <br /> All formerly human supernaturals can be described using certain common qualities: they process that permanently makes them inherently magical damages their soul, with damage being roughly proportionate to how powerful they are. This soul damage spreads and festers, and it must be counteracted using some sort of substitute. Vampires hold on to fragments of humanity. Werewolves have The Hunt. Mages use their Obsessions to fill the holes in their souls. Changelings seek remnants of their lost humanity, but also use narrative roles and archetypes. Sin-Eaters have their Geist holding them together. Mummies have servitude to their cult and the Judges. Beasts have their Hunger. &quot;Uncategorized&quot; Deviants have whatever they find, often loyalty to an ideal or a group. <br /> <br /> &quot;Mage&quot;, &quot;Awakened&quot;, and &quot;Hollow&quot; are all blanket terms for a deviant who managed to permanently alter their own metaphysical makeup by blowing a localized hole through reality inside their soul, through obsessive pursuit of knowledge and power. <br /> <br /> This allows them to break through the Abyss, which acts as a sort of immune system for reality, and exists as the result of the Fall, an event in the distant past of uncertain nature that created the current state of earth and reality. Most Awakened believe or at least suspect that it was in some way the result of the earliest mages fucking things up really badly. <br /> <br /> Mages must fight a constant battle to balance their Obsessions with their ability to act as a functioning human being, and most inevitably retreat into exaggerated personas as a substitute for genuine human connection. <br /> <br /> Mages cannot ascend to any sort of higher state. This is because, in ChroD, there are no &quot;higher states&quot;. In a horror setting, monstrosity is the only path to power. To reach more powerful states, mages must sacrifice even more humanity and degenerate further into their personas. They can become Archmasters, True Fae-like beings (some True Fae may even be Archmasters, if the ST thinks it would be interesting) who spend most of their time hiding out in solipsistic havens. Their ability to interact with the world is greatly diminished despite their power, as they find it almost impossible to genuinely empathize with other humans, and even their most subtle manipulation risks creating destructive waves of Paradox backlash and pissed-off gods. Mages can also Ascend, but this process is best understood as being narratively similar to what happens when a ghost passes on. It might be an ascent to a higher realm, or it might just be complete cessation of existence, and the actual truth is entirely up to the ST if it ever comes up. This endlessly vexes the Silver Ladder, as the most promising path to their goal seems to inevitably destroy the sanity and eventually existence of any mage who pursues this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:53:07-07:00","id":992106,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely liking the idea of the abyss as reality's immune system that protects the world from the damage mages can do. The problem with this is that the existing examples of Intruders and Acamoth, creatures from the Abyss, are all very bad for people who encounter them and reality in general. You could just remove these or say that mages are interpreting intruders from an unreliable perspective, but it seems to require some real mental gynmnastics and gets rid of interesting threats. There's plenty of topics on the forums of how mages can curbstomp enemies of the normal rpg bestiary type. Having antiphysics equations or inescapable looping pathways that trap people can add needed unease to the experience.<br /> <br /> For your last paragraph... I dunno. It seems like most of what you have as hacked canon is already in the commonly accepted Awakening setting, just not presented in so negative a light. Ascension isn't meant to be a character upgrade, its either a background event that leaves mysteries behind or a conclusion to a PC character arc when the player is ready to leave that character behind with only memories and the ripple effects of their life as reminders. While default ascension is pretty vague, it seems clear that it is a cessation of existence, at least existence of the form that humans would recognize or understand fully in order to become both one with the cosmos and a pillar supporting it.<br /> <br /> I should mention that I do not own Mage 2e right now, so I'm going on what I know from open development and the forums for how some of this stuff is meant to be interpreted. I apologize in advance if that resutls in me completely missing the point of a particular change you want to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:57:34-07:00","id":992109,"title":"","content":"Regardless of whether or not any of this is present, it's not emphasized as much as I would like, and it still takes a lot of work to turn Mage into a personal horror game about being a monster as opposed to urban fantasy game about having magic powers. Also, as a huge fan of the various minor templates and sorcerers that we've seen across the setting, I'd like to make it clearer that mages aren't an unambiguous step up from them or anything like &quot;humanity+&quot;. Mage as it is just doesn't fit with what I want out of ChroD. It's a perfectly fine urban fantasy game in its current state, but it's not quite the personal horror game I'm looking for. Also, seriously, where are the mad scientists?<br /> <br /> Look at the differences between how becoming an archmaster is presented and viewed by the fandom versus how becoming a True Fae is presented and viewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:05:52-07:00","id":992112,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Redundant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:55:30-07:00","id":992130,"title":"","content":"Here's another description of what I'd like Mages to be: a minor template psychic is someone who happens to have psychic powers. A psychic Deviant is a freak with a bulging cranium who can barely walk down the street without setting something on fire. A minor template sorcerer is someone who practices magic. A Mage is a human-shaped hole in reality who is fundamentally incapable of perceiving reality without using the lens of their own persona, and is more likely to die and level a city block with their death spasms because they tried to replace their heart with a magical particle accelerator than to live to 30.<br /> <br /> Would it be too much to have &quot;no one can become a Mage without being a fundamentally broken person&quot; as a rule of character creation?<br /> <br /> Also, while I acknowledge that this is entirely a personal preference, I dislike that Mage is seemingly set up to encourage people to make awful dull Sarcastic British Man Who Knows Everything And Everyone Loves Him Because He Is Quirky characters. Like, Warren Ellis and Grant Morrison are good authors, but can I at least partially blame them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:10:08-07:00","id":992137,"title":"","content":"Also, as a quote for the Obsessions section, I'm gonna use:<br /> <br /> &quot;I just...I just wanted to kick his ass! I wanted to build a machine to kick his ass! I wanted to build an empire to house the machine to kick his ass!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:25:53-07:00","id":992146,"title":"","content":"I read through Genius a few years back, and while I definitely appreciated a place in CoD/WoD for mad science, superheroics, and weird tales, the places where it tried to integrate personal horror for me fell flat because its conceits of Inspiration and the state of the Peerage vs. Unmada/Lemurians were so depressing that I wasn't enthused about the idea of playing it. Basically the question with Genius is: &quot;If nothing I do with Inspiration can ever actually advance science, uncover true knowledge, or be used to help people except on a one-on-one scale (and the Peerage PCs are supposed to believe this), why bother with it at all? I'd do just as much good teaching elementary school or planting a flower garden.&quot; But to each their own and if you want more Genius in your Awakening, then let's figure out how to make this setting work!<br /> <br /> I saw in your first couple posts that you reference and reimagine all the pentacle orders, but I love the Seers as an organization so I'd be interested in what your take on them is. Perhaps they are contacted by beings from whatever unreality fills the Hollow, with promises for a cure in exchange for managing and selectively modifying the balance between Supernal and normal reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:31:29-07:00","id":992149,"title":"","content":"I really have to disagree on your take on the default Mage character though. I'd been creating some rough character outlines for a Seer ruling council just to satisfy my creativity, and my base concepts are less Sherlock and more an unholy alliance of Frank Underwood, Big Boss/Naked Snake, and the State Alchemists from FMA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12051-kvedulf","name":"Kvedulf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:39:13-07:00","id":992152,"title":"","content":"Hey, that's great, but I've seen sooooo many variations on the concept of &quot;Too-Cool Guy Who Knows All The Things And Is Cool And British&quot;. <br /> <br /> I've always adored Genius and its hopelessness and nihilism. And, if I had the power to change ChroD in any way I could, I would either replace Mage with Genius or make it more like it. I really prefer the &quot;mages force their own delusions onto the world&quot; to &quot;mages know truths no one else knows&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, the way I see Mage, the &quot;protagonist&quot; factions are either supervillains and utopia-seeking megalomaniacs or desperate madmen trying to hold onto their sanity. The antagonists are the two extremes: either those who have given in fully to delusion or those who are so rigorously logical and unromantic that they use their magic to keep reality as strictly regulated as possible. <br /> <br /> Either the Seers or the Banishers could easily be right. It could be that magic is so inherently unstable and corrupting and dangerous that wiping it out or tightly controlling it is the only possible way to protect humanity. I want that to be not only possible but likely. Or at the very least, raise this possibility: if Mages do manage to rebuild their lost utopia...what makes them think it'll go any better than the last time? Considering what the first Fall did to reality...are they really gonna risk another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:41:24-07:00","id":992154,"title":"","content":"Okay, here we go <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1. There is an edit button at the bottom of your posts. By posting four times in a row, you don't come off as excited, you come off as someone desperately shouting &quot;look at me, notice I'm here, comment so I feel I have worth!&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2. Since Deviant isn't out and we don't have swathes of text from it describing exactly what Deviants are and how to play them, I think you are throughly preparing yourself to hate the actual setting once it drops since you're building so much headcanon around them already. <br /> <br /> 3. &quot;In a horror setting, monstrosity is the only path to power&quot;, is incredibly narrow and dull. I say this because you seem to mean literal monstrosity, being a wolf man, having vampiric canines etc. Following this philosophy means that a character such as Hannibal Lector isn't suited to be an antagonist within a Horror setting. <br /> <br /> 4. An honest question here, have you ever actually properly read any of the Mages books? Your description of how you want to modify Archmastery and Ascension would make it match what Archmastery and Ascension already is. Archmastery, as written within the available setting material is already a minor godling that lives in a solipsistic haven who is unable to wield much of their power in the real world for fear of creating massive waves of paradox and having other minor godlings pissed at them. <br /> <br /> 4. After so many of your complaints being aimed at Mage not being especially horrific, Mages just being magic powered super humans and all that, your sample quote on Obsessions seems rather lacking. A Mage obsessed with kicking some opponents ass using a super weapon he built, and creating an empire to allow this construction seems rather like your ideal mages are merely magically powered super villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:45:47-07:00","id":992157,"title":"","content":"Also, I've found that it's fairly easy to use Awakening to support Paradigms: the Supernal is a vast unrefined singularity of infinite potential and magical energy, but the only way to harness it or enter it is to force order on it. Yantras do this, Shadow Names and Personas do this, and all magical procedures are essentially limits that the Mage forces into the Supernal to be able to draw it into the Phenomenal without annihilating it. <br /> <br /> The original Awakening only gives us five paths, but I'd say those are only the most common ones. An Awakening is a hyper-personal experience, where the Mage forces an image of their own construction on the raw chaos of the Supernal, and that image forever colors their magic, and their perception of reality. As an example, an Acanthus can never not see the world through the lens of Time and Fate. They can never see anything without seeing it first as the archetype it represents. A surgeon who Awakens through that lens will forever primarily perceive everything, everything as a collection of organs. The Monarch can never not be The Monarch.<br /> <br /> And okay, I'll do more editing than posting again. I'm not sure that I'm preparing myself to hate Deviant, when everything I've seen about it looks good. What's your basis for saying that? I personally dislike some elements of one thing Dave wrote, so therefore I'll inevitably hate anything else he writes? I don't even think Awakening is bad or flawed or poorly written, it's just not specifically what I want. <br /> <br /> I don't mean literal monstrosity. I don't know where you got that from. I love Hunter, and I think it does that well. For example, a TFV agent might never be anything other than 100% unenhanced human, but rising in the ranks inevitably requires them to do shady, awful things and suborn their personal values to a vast and uncaring bureaucracy. Also, Hannibal does not have superpowers. I'm specifically talking about supernatural power. If you have &quot;good powers vs evil powers&quot;, you don't have horror, at least not to me. I prefer that, in a horror setting, all sources of supernatural power should be inherently dangerous and corrupting. <br /> <br /> And supervillains is fine as the niche for mages. I've mentioned Genius, and if Mage is there, I'd like it to be something like that, the mad scientists and supervillains line. And I'm going to do the &quot;have you actually read it&quot; thing to you. Have you actually watched The Venture Brothers? The Monarch is an utterly broken man completely consumed by his own obsessions. That's my ideal Mage. His desire to kick Dr. Venture's ass is a perfect example of an obsession. <br /> <br /> I have read the books. I'm aware that a lot of what I want is already there, I just want to emphasize it more. Go back to where I mentioned the difference between how the fandom perceives archmasters vs True Fae. <br /> <br /> Also, about point one? Here's a bit of advice. Don't lead with stuff like that. It doesn't make people want to listen to what you say. I say that as someone who had to realize the hard way that beginning criticism with &quot;okay, listen up you feculent assholes, I hate you and you're wrong&quot; does not tend to make people receptive to what you have to say. <br /> <br /> I am not interested in turning this into another argument. I have my opinion and I know what I want. That might be different from yours, which is fine. I'm done with fighting and arguing. I have spent too much time in the mud, screaming and throwing shit at people who disagreed with me and picking fights over nothing, and it got me nowhere. I am extending my policy on Promethean to Mage: I will not complain about it, or argue about it, or speak negatively about it at all. If I have done that, tell me and I will edit it. From here on outward, I am interested only in doing productive things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:15:33-07:00","id":992174,"title":"","content":"If you don't want critique, nor apparently even a dialogue, why are you posting on a forum? You also asked me to comment on my points, but then ended your post saying you don't want to discus anything, just be told how to write your version of Mage. You kind of don't leave much room there, I either ignore your questions and seem like an ass for not providing explanation for what I said to you, or ignore your directive to not talk in any way that isn't writing material for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:54:19-07:00","id":992190,"title":"","content":"So, let me get this straight:<br /> <br /> You want something completely different from what <i>Mage 2e</i> is, you shit on its setting, you lash out at everyone trying to help you, and you constantly promote a (poorly designed) fansplat on the official forum for the main game, insult the people trying to engage with you, and then demand people design new mechanics for you.<br /> <br /> If you don't like <i>Mage 2e</i>'s mechanics design your own mechanics, or do the work to update the fansplat you really want yourself. Don't tell a bunch of fans of the real game that if it were up to you it'd be completely different, because then the response you're going to get is &quot;glad it wasn't left up to you, because your ideas suck and you clearly don't know what you're doing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:03:16-07:00","id":992193,"title":"","content":"You probably would make a lot more progress if you just found some people who like Genius and not Mage and then went to discuss how to do what you want somewhere private instead of continuing to flaunt your dissatisfaction with the game right in the faces of the people who are here to enjoy discussing the actual game.<br /> <br /> I mean, you say no argument, but basically all of your posts are just begging to start them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:28:42-07:00","id":992209,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Woah, guys, take it easy. I know there is a lot of frustration surrounding Gecko's conduct on the forums lately, but coming into her homebrew thread to berrate her for her headcannon is not cool. She has been on very thin ice lately, but ever since I told her it was her last warning, she has been making a serious effort to focus on creating her own homebrew instead of bashing on the canon setting. We should extend the same courtesy to her that we expect her to show us. Mages as supervillains is the buy-in for this homebrew. If you're not into it, you don't have to participate in it. But don't come into the thread just to talk shit and start another fight. That's threadcrapping at best and harassment at worst.<br /> <br /> Also, Gecko, please lay off the &quot;Mage is Urban Fantasy/isn't horror&quot; and the jibes about Intelligent Quirky British Characters. They're a big part of what's inciting people to come into the thread and argue with you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-23-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:40:31-07:00","id":992213,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how I'm doing half of the things I'm being accused of, and the other half are subjective. For example, saying that my ideas suck is subjective (after all, I can concede that my criticisms of Mage and other games are subjective as well, and I've stopped trying to I've been an asshole in the past about things, but I'm trying not to be here. <br /> <br /> I have not shit on the game anywhere in this thread. Have you noticed how every time I have raised a problem I had with the game, I've followed it up with a qualifier that I'm only referring to my preference? &quot;This doesn't really fit in with my personal ChroD canon&quot; is a completely subjective statement. If you genuinely believe that I do not know my own opinions, and Mage actually fits perfectly with what I want out of ChroD, I would be happy to hear you explain how you came to that conclusion. &quot;Mage is a perfectly well designed game that isn't horror-y enough for me&quot; is another subjective statement. And it's one you haven't even addressed other than to say &quot;stop saying it&quot;. You haven't told me why you consider it wrong. I'll stop mentioning british cumberbatch fishmalks anyway, but if any of you have particular objections to me criticizing them, I'd be happy to hear those as well. <br /> <br /> I'm going to be brutally honest. You didn't give me anything. You didn't give me any useful criticism or suggestions. You just raised subjective problems you had with my outlook and asked questions that don't lead anywhere (like, &quot;have you actually read the books?&quot;) Every time someone has given me useful criticism or suggestions, I have responded to them. You are not doing any of that. &quot;Genius sucks, stop mentioning it&quot; is not productive. Why should I not block you? What productive feedback are you giving me, beyond &quot;I don't like what you're doing, stop doing it&quot;?<br /> <br /> I don't want this to turn into what happened on the old thread, and that's what I'm saying. I'm not interested in arguing any more. If you think my posts are &quot;begging&quot; to start, that's on you. I have taken pains after earlier arguments to repeatedly say that this is a matter of opinion and preference. <br /> <br /> We also came into the same problem with half the people saying that what I want is already there and half of them saying that what I want is radically different. Before you dispute that as you always have, look back at the posts. Gullinbursti told me that something I wanted was already there and questioned if I had read the books, but then proindrakenzol told me that what I want is completely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:42:20-07:00","id":992216,"title":"","content":"Apologies. My post wasn't meant to be antagonistic, my initial point may have been construed as such, but I was attempting to point out what is seen as common courtesy in the majority of forums. I wasn't trying to say &quot;okay, listen up you feculent assholes, I hate you and you're wrong&quot;, but being told only to reply to a thread in certain ways is rather limiting when it comes to explaining a misunderstood intent.<br /> <br /> Edit: 'aight, I'll explain my questions as best as I can <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With Deviant, the reason I said you seem to be building yourself towards a fall is you were using the capitalised Deviant, while talking about supernaturals within the setting. At the moment, we really don't know how well Deviants will map to the other splats. Since your main issue with Mage is that it doesn't map well to how you envision horror, I'd say, at a guess, that it won't map to exactly what you want since you aren't the one writing it. This, like in the case of Mage, would most likely create a tonal dissonance with what the setting will actually provide when compared to the canon you are already creating.<br /> <br /> With the comparison of forms of horror, your writing seems to indicate you want there to be massively negative impacts on the characters, in this case, Mages being soulless monstrosities who can only see the world viewed through a lens provided by their Arcana. This seemed to imply that you view horror as requiring some sort of physical or mental deformity for their to actually be horror within a setting. To me this seems rather limiting in that it denies mundane horror, the horror of humanity, which limits your setting quite a bit.<br /> <br /> When I questioned if you'd read the Mage books, I guess I more meant, &quot;the majority of mage books&quot; because reading through material you've written, I'm not the only one who has pointed out that some of the material you've highlighted as wanting to exist within your version of the setting, already exists. For example, you mentioned Archmastery and then described what you'd like it to be. Your example of what it should be like pretty much directly used the material as its already written. There's no shame in not having read every Mage book, or even just forgetting a segment, but as someone reading what you write, it makes your writing seem confused when I read a statement that says an aspect of Mage should be changed to what it already is.<br /> <br /> With my final point, I was mainly highlighting it because thematically super villains and heroes don't map out differently enough for me to see where you divide them. With the complaint about Mages being magically powered heroes, I can't personally see where the idea of magically powered super villains is distinct enough from the former to become a cornerstone for a complete rewriting of the Mage setting. Rather than changing canon here in a rewritten setting, this seems a minor element of the game that would be reinforced merely by the tone used by the ST when describing scenes within his game.<br /> <br /> Oh, and finally, a new note. In general it makes it difficult to talk about what you've said if you do things like edit your own posts to remove what was previously said. By removing what you'd written about Archmastery and how you envisioned it, when someone like myself attempts to use it within their own posting, it can seem like an attempt to modify your own statements to win over an audience in an argument. I'm not trying to imply this was your intent in this case, but since the statement wasn't contentious, nor asked to be removed by a moderator, it can seem so. (I'm sure we've all seen examples online where someone has written something like &quot;Children Soldiers are cool&quot;, waited for an outcry against it and then modified the initial statement to something like &quot;Women's rights are something we should all get behind&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 10-24-2016, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:47:01-07:00","id":992219,"title":"","content":"So, are you saying I was in the wrong in saying I didn't want this thread to turn into another argument like the last one? &quot;Don't make multiple posts&quot; is constructive criticism, but putting it the way you did and then following it up with a three-poster dogpile basically telling me &quot;stop doing and saying things because we don't agree with them&quot; does not do a good job of establishing good intentions.<br /> <br /> I acknowledge that some of the things I said weren't constructive and were needlessly antagonistic. I can kind of see where you're coming from, because I know what it's like to lash out in frustration. I went back to lashing out at Mage in frustration for not being what I wanted. I have edited the posts in question. <br /> <br /> I mean, I would at least have been satisfied if you had actually explained why you think I'm wrong and Mage is horror and not just dark urban fantasy. &quot;Mage doesn't feel like personal horror as it is&quot; is as subjective a statement as &quot;Genius is poorly designed&quot; or &quot;Gecko's ideas suck&quot;, and it's actually a less inflammatory one. I mean, what's more polite? &quot;This game is perfectly well designed but its current form isn't exactly what I would prefer&quot; or &quot;you suck and you like bad things&quot;?<br /> <br /> I am trying to be better when it comes to acknowledging opinions, and I know it is somewhat hypocritical of me to complain about people claiming their opinions as objective truth. But I'm trying to do better. It doesn't help, though, that the people who are disagreeing based on preference rarely explain why they feel that way. I have actually explained why Mages don't feel monstrous enough, and how it conflicts thematically with crossovers with the wider setting and makes minor templates feel pointless. You will note that this is an entirely subjective argument. For example, if you don't care about crossovers or minor templates, it doesn't matter at all, and that's valid. If you don't think Mage clashes thematically compared to the other splats and doesn't overshadow minor templates, that's valid. If you think that, and think that I'm wrong about it and shouldn't feel that way, could you at least tell me why you feel that way instead of just saying &quot;you're wrong&quot;? To give one example, I made a thread asking if I was wrong to feel like mages were objectively better than minor template sorcerers in a way that other major templates weren't privileged over minor templates, and I didn't really get an answer. I've said that I don't like that the most human splat is the most powerful. I have yet to see anyone explain why mages aren't actually the most human splat, or aren't the most powerful, or why it's okay for the most human splat to be the most powerful. <br /> <br /> And proin, I would like you to explain, here or in PM, exactly how I did each of the things you're accusing me of, so that I can avoid doing them in the future. Keeping in mind that I've addressed several of them: <br /> <br /> 1. Saying that something isn't as crossover viable or dark as I prefer is not &quot;shitting on the setting&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. Genius' quality is subjective. Actually, could you tell me what you think makes it poorly designed? Because I would agree with you that the game mechanics are something of a mess. That's one of the reasons why I switched to Awakening, in fact. So if we agree that the mechanics are a pain, that brings us to the setting and themes, and that's entirely subjective. Genius being darker and emphasizing futility more than you would like is not an objective flaw. I have been trying to do better at admitting that the things I do not like are not objective truths. I have said several times in this thread that I consider Mage well designed and have indicated that I have learned that it isn't flawed just because it doesn't fit my preferences. <br /> <br /> And <br /> <br /> 3. &quot;Demanding people make rules for you&quot; is essentially you trying to make me sound like a jerk for saying &quot;can we do productive things instead of just telling me I'm wrong and should stop&quot; or &quot;does anyone have any ideas?&quot; You attack me for not accepting feedback, but then you attack me for asking for feedback and suggestions.<br /> <br /> And also? The reason I reacted so angrily was because almost everything you brought up has already been addressed. I have explained many times why I'm working with Mage. <br /> <br /> And the real reason why it bothers me that half of the people tell me that what I want is already there and half of them say it's a radical departure (apart from the fact that neither faction has explained why they think this) is that despite both sides having seemingly diametrically opposed opinions on Mage, they never seem to argue with each other about them, and only use them as a cudgel against me. <br /> <br /> &quot;Mage is already a personal horror game about monsters! Shut up!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I agree with you! Making Mage a personal horror about monsters would be too radical a departure! Gecko should shut up!&quot;<br /> <br /> And as an aside &quot;mages as supervillains&quot; isn't the big-in. &quot;Mages are cursed monsters with holes in reality drilled through their souls teetering on the brink of madness, and also a lot of them are mad scientists&quot; is. The supervillain thing is actually completely optional, it's just a great demonstration of the whole &quot;creating an exaggerated persona to compensate for your inner emptiness&quot; theme. If you don't want Mages wearing tights and masks and cackling, that's perfectly viable even within this project. If you don't want mages being mad scientists at all, or being warped walking holes in reality, than I don't really understand your views but I respect them and won't argue with them. If you don't like The Monarch as an example, how about Walter White? He's a much more realistic and down to earth character, but he's another absolutely perfect example of the kinds of characters and stories I'm looking for from Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:21:07-07:00","id":992239,"title":"","content":"No, I can completely understand why you don't want endless arguments. However, limiting the way people can reply, and demanding no negative feedback or discussion of the preexisting canon limits the ability to provide any commentary on your setting hack. I know you don't want endless negativity, and I'm not advocating that people enter the thread merely to lambast you with their hatred of your preferred interpretation of the material. However, a complete lack of negative feedback means you remove the ability for flaws in your setting to come to light through discussion, there is a reason editors, line developers and creative consultants exist.<br /> <br /> Also, it wasn't my intent to inspire an attack against you. I know two others jumped in and commented, but it wasn't an organised effort in any way. If you have a look at the other times I've interacted with you, I do my best to be pretentiously civil despite my own overweening arrogance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: On #3 above, I can't provide excessive explanation of what I was driving at since you modified the post. However, my memory of it was something like &quot;I don't want negative feedback, arguments, references to canon. All I want is positive feedback and help creating the setting&quot;. As I said above, that seemed rather limiting and that you did only want there to be mechanical help with creating material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 10-24-2016, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:48:40-07:00","id":992248,"title":"","content":"I did not demand that people not mention previous canon or give any negative feedback. I apologize if you read that, and I have edited earlier posts to better communicate. I will say that I never said &quot;I only want positive feedback&quot; or &quot;no references to canon&quot;. I said that I only wanted constructive feedback.<br /> <br /> To try to bring things back on track, inspirational media is also welcome. <br /> <br /> So far, I have:<br /> <br /> Birdman (an incredible depiction of an Awakening) <br /> <br /> Fullmetal Alchemist (not that horror-y, but very well done and with some appropriately dark revelations about the setting)<br /> <br /> The Venture Brothers (a beautiful depiction of obsession, futility, and shadow societies of broken people lost in their own personas)<br /> <br /> Breaking Bad (even though it's known primarily as a gritty crime drama, Breaking Bad is probably one of the best explorations of the psychology of the mad scientist ever made)<br /> <br /> Worm (one of the countless dark superhero deconstructions, any of which could provide material. Worm, however, has a lot of twisty cosmic horror material and mysteries that make it one of the best fits)<br /> <br /> Genius: The Transgression (if you don't like Genius, you probably won't like The Hollow Chronicle. Mad scientists, futility, and broken people frantically struggling for an impossible utopia abound in both.)<br /> <br /> Re-Animator (one of the classic mad scientist films) <br /> <br /> The Prestige (two stage magicians and weird science-dabblers are caught up in an obsessive rivalry, which fits THC pretty well)<br /> <br /> Jojo's Bizarre Adventure (what, you're playing ChroD and you haven't read JJBA?)<br /> <br /> Dorohedoro (a weird fantasy series with pitch-black humor about two parallel worlds and the freaks and wizards who inhabit them. The magic here is primarily a device used to explore the characters and their world, but there's a complicated occult mystery at the heart of it, surrounding an amnesiac assassin with the head of a lizard and a man living inside his mouth)<br /> <br /> Dr. Faustus (one of the classic stories of sorcerous hubris)<br /> <br /> The Tempest (another classic tale of sorcery)<br /> <br /> Unknown Armies (probably the greatest occult-themed rpg ever made)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T22:02:01-07:00","id":992259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=992248#post992248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not demand that people not mention previous canon or give any negative feedback. I apologize if you read that, and I have edited earlier posts to better communicate. I will say that I never said &quot;I only want positive feedback&quot; or &quot;no references to canon&quot;. I said that I only wanted constructive feedback. When you fight with someone, your mind subconsciously tries to see them in the worst possible light. I know that from experience, and I know you have to fight that. Remembering &quot;only constructive feedback&quot; as &quot;only positive feedback&quot; is an example of that. An angry mind warps and twists and everything it sees so that it can continue to be angry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't imply that my memory is that faulty, I'm neither mad with rage nor derangement and implying I am is incredibly insulting either way I read it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=992248#post992248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To try to bring things back on track, inspirational media is also welcome. I won't even ban 3edgy5u smug britishman media, as oversaturated as I think it is when it comes to Mage. I'll even suppress my rant about how The Dresden Files is derivative misogynistic crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character Dresden, despite the name, is an American character. Also, deriding it as &quot;derivative misogynistic crap&quot; while asking for others not to insult you or your setting comes across as rather disingenuous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:31:59-07:00","id":992317,"title":"","content":"Sorry if my last post came across as inflammatory. It wasn't supposed to be exclusionary but a suggestion for proceeding that might result in catching less flak.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd still say you don't really have to change anything since it's about how the story plays out that really drives a point home. For instance you provide NPCs modeled off of Venture Brothers and your characters will face enormous difficulties in trying to make positive changes to the setting. Heck, anyone not sinking further into their exaggerated personas could be derided as not taking their condition seriously enough. Rebellion against this status quo would inevitably force them into a &quot;different&quot; kind of exaggerated persona as a result of negative peer pressure. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T05:00:36-07:00","id":992333,"title":"","content":"Y'know, I think you could easily build a RAW mage who does a decent Genius impression. Instead of overt magical displays, they just use low-level forces and matter to tweak physics and make impossible devices viable.<br /> <br /> Need a material stronger than anything in reality? No problem! <br /> <br /> Radiation getting you down? Veil that sucker!<br /> <br /> SCIENCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T06:28:53-07:00","id":992353,"title":"","content":"Speaking as a British guy who has ample quirks and is smarter than you, I had been assuming that your occasional references to same were another semi-veiled personal attack. But if it's just an hyperbolic dislike of Doctor Who and Sherlock, carry on.<br /> <br /> And we finally agree on something, gecko.<br /> <br /> The Dresden Files *are* rather less original, and for that matter well-written, than they're made out to be.<br /> <br /> (Early on in 2e's open development a small, deluded group of people accused us if stealing Mage Sight from Dresden. Which given it's glorified oWoD fanfic is rather rich)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:42:50-07:00","id":992379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=992353#post992353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dresden Files *are* rather less original, and for that matter well-written, than they're made out to be.<br /> <br /> (Early on in 2e's open development a small, deluded group of people accused us if stealing Mage Sight from Dresden. Which given it's glorified oWoD fanfic is rather rich)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck I'm tired of the Dresden Files, like holy fuck they make me physically exhausted to hear about.<br /> <br /> I managed to slog through those books, dragging myself through them while suppressing my desire to cast them into the fire or point out that they are literally oWoD wearing a funny hat.<br /> <br /> I remember those &quot;oh but you stole mage sight from dresden files&quot; complaints, and they are as laughable now as they were back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:31:53-07:00","id":992393,"title":"","content":"I like the Dresden Files. However, they're hardly the epitome of award winning classic fiction (along with virtually all other modern urban fantasy and horror genre fiction mostly targeting teens and young adults), and that's certainly not a requirement for the books to still be a fun and relaxing diversion.<br /> <br /> I've also sometimes used the series as inspiration for both old and new WOD/CofD chronicles. Nevertheless, the Dresden Files is its own setting and constantly trying to force it to conform to Mage or other gamelines (or vice-versa) leads to nothing but needless contention and disappointment. Enjoy them both (or not) on their own merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:52:02-07:00","id":992399,"title":"","content":"For the record, if I ever compare ChroD or WoD stuff to the Dresden files, it's probably <i>not</i> going to be a complaint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:37:00-07:00","id":992459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=992353#post992353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as a British guy who has ample quirks and is smarter than you, I had been assuming that your occasional references to same were another semi-veiled personal attack. But if it's just an hyperbolic dislike of Doctor Who and Sherlock, carry on.<br /> <br /> And we finally agree on something, gecko.<br /> <br /> The Dresden Files *are* rather less original, and for that matter well-written, than they're made out to be.<br /> <br /> (Early on in 2e's open development a small, deluded group of people accused us if stealing Mage Sight from Dresden. Which given it's glorified oWoD fanfic is rather rich)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm editing out the various complaints about that, because yeah, they weren't productive at all. And I really promise you that it wasn't intended as a personal attack against you. I can see that given earlier times in which I attacked you, that could be your perception, but I really didn't mean it that way. And for the record, I don't consider you to be part of that category, since among other reasons you are a real person instead of a derivative fictional character. And I don't even have any problems with you quirks or you being smarter than me (subjective, though I doubt that I ever could have come up with Mage's magic system or Deviant's mechanics). That said, that part does read kind of like deliberate provocation. I'm trying not to do that, but I'd prefer that others didn't as well. <br /> <br /> And I think we agree on more than just being tired of the Dresden Files, though that's nice to hear as well!<br /> <br /> Anyway, this was entirely on me. Sorry for derailing my own thread by letting pointless grudges seep into my posts again. I looked back to earlier posts, and I see know that what happened yesterday wouldn't have happened if I had been more civil. Sorry, everyone. I've been trying to be more positive and productive, but I guess I didn't make it this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:42:21-07:00","id":992468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981889-gecko-s-awakening-hack-take-two?p=992459#post992459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I think we agree on more than just disliking the Dresden Files, though that's nice to hear as well!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe Dave dislikes the Dresden Files, rather he acknowledges that it's not particularly original and it's certainly not Shakespeare. Nevertheless, there are a lot of derivative and average creative endeavors that are still quite enjoyable, as nearly every recent movie out of Hollywood can attest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:59:04-07:00","id":992480,"title":"","content":"Alright, edited to make sure I wasn't assuming too much. <br /> <br /> Again, Dave, I don't hate or even dislike you. One of many reasons for that is that if I couldn't rail against you without being gigantically hypocritical, because I'm not currently in a place to accuse anyone else of being insulting and condescending. I can't wag my finger at you, because I've done everything I could accuse you of far more often (I can't exactly act shocked and offended for you saying you're smarter than me, because of how often I've taken the &quot;I'm right and you're wrong and this is empirical truth&quot; position. In fact, the fact that I immediately zeroed in on that part of your post as a personal attack against me, when it was likely just sarcastically using the wording I had used, says a lot about me, and indicates that I'm still in the mode of looking for fights with people). If I write you off as an asshole for disagreeing with me and having different ideas, then I can't exactly complain when other people do that with me. Not to mention, all of the massively worse people there are out there.<br /> <br /> I apologize again for being overly negative, unproductive, and confrontational. <br /> <br /> Back on track, about the &quot;cursed&quot; theme and establishing that Awakened are not &quot;humans but better&quot;, there are some ways to establish it. I want to make it super clear that Awakening is not a reward or a sign of virtue or even ability, and obsessive pursuit of a goal beyond the limits of sanity is the most likely way to reach it. Being a moral person, a determined person, or even an intelligent or creative person does not make you more likely to Awaken. As an example, Stephen Hawking is unlikely to Awaken, because when one of his theories is proven wrong he accepts it and keeps going instead of screaming &quot;No, you're wrong!&quot; at the universe. Awakening comes to those people willing to burn their clothes and lock themselves in a shed for weeks to tattoo lines from the Iliad on their bodies to protect themselves from the chemtrail goblins. Another thing I'm borrowing from Genius is that it's very hard for the Awakened to make genuine lasting contributions to human history, society, and culture. (Genius gives Da Vinci and Nikola Tesla as examples of the few historical figures who were likely Geniuses, and they could easily have been Mages). This is part of the overall philosophy of ChroD, if I'm not mistaken, and I always thought Mage made it a bit too easy to say that all or most of human history is the result of magical manipulation (though I liked that Mage Noir made it clear that mages didn't invent the atom bomb). Going back to what I said about awakening, mages tend to have a very hard time functioning in normal human culture. The Seers are the ones who are the best at it. <br /> <br /> About the Seers, I kind of like the idea that they're actually less numerous than the other factions, and I'll put it in the storytelling section as a potential reveal the ST could pull. Mages are meant to be fairly rare, and I also like the idea that the Seers use subtle and far-reaching manipulation to indirectly influence people, and deliberately play on Awakened paranoia to make themselves seem larger and more omnipresent than they really are. Part of the retooled Seers is that they're very aware of how warped and broken the Awakened are, and they use that to their advantage: deliberately seeding clues to play into the Obsessions of Pentacle mages who try to follow them, until those mages start seeing Seer agents and plants everywhere. <br /> <br /> I was struggling with what to do with the Free Council, since they've always been a bit of a stumbling block for me (too many fans portray them as unambiguously good gee whiz too hip science heroes), and I've decided to give them a major and explicit connection to organized crime, to the point of having their internal organization closely resemble the mafia, pirate crews, and other criminal organizations. This is the model they use to influence Sleeper culture, similarly to the way the Diamond uses mystery cults and fraternal organizations. <br /> <br /> I also want to introduce a &quot;Nemesis&quot; condition, representing a character having a Venture Bros-style &quot;arch&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:46:19-07:00","id":992708,"title":"","content":"Currently stuck on how to work out the Tremere and archmasters. I kind of like the idea that all archmastery is basically a form of lichdom, since ChroD is all about exploring monster archetypes. Here's one nerf I'm considering for archmasters based on that idea: each archmaster has an object called a Phylactery. They can only manifest in the physical world with one, or else they start causing major paradox backlash almost immediately. Destroying it bars them from the world until they can use Quintessence to make another one. Destroying an archmage's phylactery inside their realm, while difficult, permanently kills them.<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone know the relative power level of archmasters, as compared to, say, the True Fae? I'd like them to be roughly equal when it comes to power, with the main difference being that archmages can't influence the world as easily as the Gentry can (assuming both exist. If only archmages exist, then sure, have them fill the role of the Gentry).<br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to emphasize the visual bang you can get out of spells and nimbuses. Since they're invisible to normals and they can look like whatever the player wants, why not give emphasize how cool they can look? In fact, mental image already has a strong connection to spellcasting, so I'll play that up, make it so that a Mage's spells appear in a way resonant with their paradigm, and this appearance is vital to even being able to cast them: an Obrimos who saw the vast machinery of the cosmos when she Awakened can't not make golden gears appear when she casts a spell. Or, to put it another way, she can't effect reality without imagining golden gears, and because the reactor of magical potential burning inside her works by turning symbols into reality, actual golden gears appear. <br /> <br /> I prefer nimbuses to be pretty dramatic by default. &quot;Moros might cause subtle rot around them, or melancholy. &quot; I get that Awakening often goes for subtlety, and that's cool, but a nimbus is a magic effect only supernatural beings can see. If you asked me to give an example of a Moros Nimbus, I would say: &quot;The skin appears to rot off her bones, and her skeleton snaps, reforms, and sprouts extra bony limbs like a grotesque undead tree. In the moment she casts the spell, she is visually transfigured into the image of a multi-armed and horned skeleton dripping with black tar. Thin black veins shoot out from the fingertips of her bony form, piercing her target and pumping the rot that surrounds her into them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I probably would have loved Mage from the beginning if someone had told me I could totally make it Persona, since even in the base rules there's nothing that says a Nimbus can manifest as the Mage summoning an ephemeral being that represents their inner self. <br /> <br /> I don't want to say &quot;I have trouble with Mage because I'm autistic&quot;, but I am, and that would pretty much be the shorter version of &quot;I have trouble with Mage because it's so frustrating trying to fit every game and setting element in ChroD into one single perfect organized, internally consistent and perfectly balanced crossover setting where everything is explained and everything has its own perfect thematic niche, and that I can't is not a negative reflection on the design of the games or on their creators, but I just can't get over my frustration over not being able to make all the pieces fit ahhhhhhh&quot;.<br /> <br /> Something I feel perfectly justified in ranting about, however, is the fact that &quot;autistic&quot; has been so widely used as an insult that I still feel awkward using it to describe myself. I hate that we're still in this fucking Victorian mindset where being neuroatypical is seen as something shameful and temporary. But that's off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-24-2016, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T20:50:09-07:00","id":992740,"title":"","content":"Big news! I'm canceling this project, and I couldn't be happier. I forced myself to confront some truths that I had been ignoring in my pursuit of a Perfect Coherent Balanced Setting. I realized that I want three different things. 1. I want to play a minor template sorcerer or mad scientist or a Deviant. 2. I want to play Mage, but not bogged down by my own desire to force it into crossover viability and thematic horror purity. 3. I want an over the top superhero game based on The Venture Bros. So I'm not longer trying to force Awakening to be all of those things. <br /> <br /> My new project is to let Awakening be Awakening. I have revised my personal canon, so that mages do not exist in my ChroD setting. The only sorcerers there are desperate hedge mages, because that was what I preferred to mages in that setting and trying to force mages to be that just wasn't working. I'm now making Mage its own setting, one in which Mage reigns supreme and I can go all out with its mad, brilliant ideas. I've made another thread for it, but basically my new Mage hack and new project is an anti-crossover: it outlines a world and cosmology defined purely by the Supernal, where the focus is entirely on the Awakened and their adventures. <br /> <br /> I'm jettisoning a lot of the rules that have been proposed or formulated to make mages more monstrous or less powerful or make the game grittier. The Awakened get to be the Awakened, not my attempt to force them into basically being a minor template. I might carry over a few of the ideas here, like weird science and path flexibility, but mostly I'm focusing on letting Mage be Mage. Letting Awakening be the most Awakeningy it can be. <br /> <br /> It's been to long. I've spent too long lying to myself about Mage and telling myself that it's a bad game, or even one I don't personally like. I've spent too long condemning it for not fitting a very narrow expectation. I'm done with that. It's time to revel in Mage for what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}